      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Silent Failures"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Missing provider yields the default value with no error",
            "null/undefined default + throwing hook catches it at once",
            "Duplicate context objects: default despite a Provider being present"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wrong Tool For The Job"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Server data in context means hand-rolled caching and staleness bugs",
            "No request dedupe, no revalidation — use a query library"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reducer Mutation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// broken: same reference, React bails out",
            "state.items.push(x); return state;",
            "// fixed:",
            "return {...state, items:[...state.items, x]};"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rules Of Hooks",
          "items": [
            "Calling useContext conditionally breaks the rules",
            "React 19 use(Ctx) is the legal conditional read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two More Mistakes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deriving an expensive value in every consumer duplicates the work",
            "Compute it once in the provider and pass the result down",
            "Over-splitting early: five contexts for values that change together",
            "That is ceremony with zero re-render benefit"
          ]
        },
